Z||000000||Chris McDonald||06-30-2001||06:25 PM||||ATTENTION:  All those that think they know how to drive a Fiero.<P>If you live in North Florida ,Georgia, or South Carolina, PLEASE make plans to bring your Fiero to the next SCCA Solo II event on July 29th in Savannah.  The Buccaneer chapter of the SCCA solo II event will be putting on event 6.  I will provide the web address below for more information.  This will be the best $20 or $25 you have ever spent in connection with your automotive hobby.<P>Just think, upward of 60 seconds of high performance driving without Johny Law in the rear view.  Way better than trying for 15 seconds of fame at the 1/4 mile.  <P>Here is the deal.  If you visit the home page, you will see this is a sport dominated by rice burners and european specialties. Of the last five events, I only saw one Fiero.  <P>This is your chance to see how that car really handles next to everything else. Put your money where your mouth is.  Don't let me down.  I am counting on seeing at least five or six of you there.  <P>(maybe we will get a Fiero pic posted on the event page)<P>Take a look at the hi-lights of event 5 picture #3.  That is my wife in the green Corvette.  Those of you that know me, know that I do not have a Fiero myself at the present.  Thus, your support will be really appreciated. <P>BE THERE.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.buccaneersolo.org" TARGET=_blank>www.buccaneersolo.org</A> <P>||||reg||6
